---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SectionLabel from '../../components/editorial/SectionLabel.astro';
import { industries } from '../../data/industries';
---

<Layout title="Industries | Trustora" description="Trustora’s EoR and Employee Intelligence capabilities for technology, science, computing, manufacturing, finance, and mission teams." currentPath="/industries/">
  <section class="page-hero"><div class="measure page-hero-grid"><div class="page-hero-copy"><SectionLabel>Industry context</SectionLabel><h1>Where the work is difficult, context matters.</h1><p>Trustora helps companies employ specialist people across borders with an operating model shaped around the work, the country, and the employee experience.</p></div><div class="page-hero-note">AI · ML · quantum · physics · science · software · mission</div></div></section>
  <section class="section cream-field"><div class="measure"><div class="section-head"><div><SectionLabel>The industry index</SectionLabel><h2 class="mt-2">Start with the work, not the job title.</h2></div><p>The same employment model can feel very different around a researcher, an engineer, a product builder, or a regulated operator.</p></div><div class="industry-index">{industries.map((industry) => <a class="industry-row" href={`/industries/${industry.slug}/`}><span class="industry-row-number">{industry.number}</span><span><h3>{industry.title}</h3><p>{industry.short}</p></span><span class="industry-row-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>)}</div></div></section>
  <section class="section dark-field"><div class="measure split-argument"><h2>Capability without context is only a list.</h2><div class="prose"><p>Our Employee Intelligence position starts with the technical and scientific reality of the role. The EoR layer then makes the local employment relationship clear enough for the person and the company to operate with confidence.</p><p>Explore a sector or <a href="/eor-brief/">request the EoR operating brief</a> for a broader decision map.</p></div></div></section>
</Layout>
